      "biography": {
        "type": "String",
        "label": "Biography",
        "value": "<p>The Borgrad Bandogge is a huge, dark-brown Ostlander dog bred to act as a night-guard. Typically chained up during the day to ensure strangers are not mauled, the short-haired war dogs are let loose each evening to kill anything foolish enough to enter the village or farm at night. In times of war, Bandogges are used extensively by Ostlander hundsmen, who bring them in small packs to the battlefield.</p>\n<p><strong>Commonly Owned By:</strong>&nbsp;Cavalryman, Guard, Outlaw</p>"
      },
